  "full_text": "Leaves are falling all around. It's time I was on my way. Thanks to you, much obliged. Such a pleasant stay. Now it's time for me to go. The autumn moon lights my way. For now I smell the rain and with it pain. And it's headed my way. Ah, sometimes I grow so tired. Now's the time, the time is now to sing my song. Going around the world, I've got to find my girl on my way. Been this way ten years to the day. Ramble on to find the queen of all my dreams. Got no time for spreading roots. The time has come to be gone. And though our health we drink a thousand times, it's time to ramble on. I ain't telling no lie. Mine's a tale that can't be told. My freedom I hold dear. How years ago and days of old, when magic filled the air. Just in the darkest depths of murder. I met a girl so fair. But Gollum, the evil one, crept up and slipped away with her. Fucking nigger. Her, yeah, nothing I can do. Guess I'll keep on repping. Guess I'll keep on rambling. Yeah. Guess I'll keep on ramblin'. Yeah, sing my song. Go around the world, gotta find my girl on my way. I've been this way ten years to the day. Ramblin' on to find the queen of all my dreams. Gotta keep searchin', baby. Baby, baby. How about that, eh?",
